        "filename": "doc/source/federation/mellon.rst",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 9098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-07-06T21:47:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can set multiple \u0027mellonIdPMetadataFile\u0027 directives when you have multiple IdPs.  You can also use a wildcard by using the \u0027MellonIdPMetadataGlob\u0027 directive.\n\nThe \u0027MellonEndpointPath\u0027 directive simply needs to be the endpoint location listed in the SP metadata for Keystone.  It does not need to be an IdP specific URL, though it does have to exist under the \u0027base\u0027 location (\u0027/v3\u0027 in this example).  I think \u0027/v3/saml2\u0027 would work fine.",
      "parentUuid": "ba3cc151_1a41b439",
      "revId": "25001ee7ffdd60c16e6fc5568765833dc16b0995",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
